38. Financial Traceability

The system should be able to trace:

Member
  ↓
Membership
  ↓
Contribution
  ↓
Payment
  ↓
Payment Attempt
  ↓
Provider Transaction
  ↓
Bank Transaction
  ↓
Reconciliation
  ↓
Ledger Entry

Not every payment will necessarily have every node in this chain.

For example, a provider callback may confirm a payment without the application directly receiving a corresponding bank transaction.

The database design must therefore preserve the distinction between:

Payment
Provider Transaction
Bank Transaction
Ledger Entry

---

39. Database Design Rule

«Do not design tables merely around screens. Design them around the real business entities and relationships.»

For example, do not create:

member_dashboard_data
payment_screen_data
loan_page_data

as database tables simply because those are frontend screens.

Instead model the actual entities:

members
memberships
contributions
payments
loans
loan_repayments
ledger_entries

The frontend should consume the domain model through APIs.

